--- 5. MAX-FLOW / MIN-CUT ANALYSIS (Edmonds-Karp) -------------
  Flow network : 6 nodes, 7 edges
  Source       : Source
  Sink         : Landfill

  Edge capacities:
      Source       -> ZoneA          8.00 t/day
      Source       -> ZoneB          8.00 t/day
      Source       -> ZoneC          8.00 t/day
      ZoneA        -> Transfer       3.00 t/day
      ZoneB        -> Transfer       3.00 t/day
      ZoneC        -> Transfer       3.00 t/day
      Transfer     -> Landfill       7.00 t/day

  Maximum feasible throughput : 7.00 t/day

  Minimum cut (bottleneck edges):
      Transfer     -> Landfill       7.00 t/day   <-- SATURATED

  The min-cut value equals the max-flow value (7.00 t/day): these edges are the
  infrastructure bottleneck that most constrains sustainable
  throughput and would govern any capacity-expansion decision.

================================================================
  Dijkstra chooses efficient paths.  Greedy prioritises urgent
  bins.  Dynamic programming respects truck capacity.  Max-flow
  exposes infrastructure bottlenecks.  One coordinated framework.
================================================================
